[heading]About this mod[/heading]

[b]Travel Between Visited Traders[/b] adds a trader dialog option for fast travel between traders you have already visited.

Talk to a trader once to record that trader. After that, choose [b]Travel to a visited trader[/b] in trader dialog and select a destination.

[b]Single-player users can install and play with the default settings.[/b]

[line]

[heading]Main features[/heading]

[list]
[*]Adds trader fast travel through dialog
[*]Only shows traders that are available from your visited-trader data
[*]Shows clean destination labels with trader name, distance, direction, and map-style coordinates
[*]Sorts destinations by distance from your current position
[*]Shows the current access mode on the destination screen
[*]Displays known vanilla and Wasteland Mod trader names cleanly when recognized
[*]Supports English and Japanese
[*]Supports single-player and multiplayer
[*]Includes multiplayer trader-sharing modes
[*]Normalizes server-side visit data to reduce duplicate destinations from older position-based records
[*]Keeps trader identity separate from the saved travel position, so slight differences in where you talked to the same trader do not create duplicate destinations
[*]Merges same-name destinations in the same trader area while keeping differently named traders separate
[*]Matches compatible raw/internal trader ID variations from older TXT/JSON data when possible
[*]Aborts travel if an unloaded destination still is not ready after preparation
[*]Preserves compatibility with older save data
[/list]

[line]

[heading]Installation[/heading]

Extract the [b]VisitedTraderTeleport[/b] folder into:

[quote]
7 Days To Die\Mods\VisitedTraderTeleport
[/quote]

The mod requires the vanilla [b]0_TFP_Harmony[/b] mod that ships with current 7 Days to Die versions.

[b]Anti-cheat should be disabled for this DLL mod.[/b]

[line]

[heading]Single-player[/heading]

No configuration is required for normal single-player use.

The default mode is [b]Personal[/b]. In single-player, that simply means you can travel to traders you have personally visited in that save.

[line]

[heading]Multiplayer[/heading]

Install this mod on both:

[list]
[*]The server
[*]Every client
[/list]

In multiplayer, the server is authoritative. The server controls which access mode is active, which traders each player may use, and whether a requested teleport is allowed.

Clients display the destination list allowed by the server.

[line]

[heading]Multiplayer access modes[/heading]

These modes are mainly for multiplayer servers. Single-player users can usually ignore this section.

[b]Default mode: Personal[/b]
If you do not change the config file, the mod uses Personal mode.

[b]Personal[/b]
Each player can travel only to traders they personally visited.

[b]Party[/b]
Players can travel to traders visited by themselves or by their current party members.

[b]Shared[/b]
Any trader visited by anyone in the active server/save data becomes available to everyone.

[line]

[heading]Configuration[/heading]

Configuration is mainly for multiplayer server owners who want to change trader-sharing behavior.

For multiplayer, edit this file on the [b]server[/b]:

[quote]
7 Days To Die\Mods\VisitedTraderTeleport\Config\VisitedTraderTeleport.xml
[/quote]

Change:

[quote]
<AccessMode value="personal" />
[/quote]

to one of:

[list]
[*]<AccessMode value="personal" />
[*]<AccessMode value="party" />
[*]<AccessMode value="shared" />
[/list]

Restart the dedicated server or host process after changing the setting.

[line]

[heading]Upgrading from version 0.2.x or older[/heading]

[b]You do not need to reset your save when upgrading.[/b]
Existing visited trader data is kept and loaded automatically.

Version [b]0.2.x and older[/b] stored visited trader data in:

[quote]
VisitedTraderTeleportVisited.txt
[/quote]

Version [b]0.3.0 and newer[/b] store new data in:

[quote]
VisitedTraderTeleportData.json
[/quote]

Upgrade behavior:

[list]
[*]Existing data is not deleted by the upgrade
[*]Existing 0.2.x-or-older TXT data continues to load after upgrading
[*]Legacy TXT data is treated as a compatibility-wide shared pool so already available destinations do not suddenly disappear
[*]Legacy TXT data is not automatically rewritten into the new ownership-aware JSON schema
[*]New visits after upgrading are recorded in the new JSON format
[*]The new format keeps trader destinations separate from player ownership, so changing between Personal, Party, and Shared later does not require resetting new-version data
[*]If old or duplicate entries are found, the mod may automatically tidy the JSON data on load while keeping player visit ownership linked to the correct trader records
[*]Version 0.4.16 and newer normalize duplicate JSON entries caused by older position-based trader keys when the matching trader area can be resolved
[*]Version 0.4.17 and newer include local trader position in normalized keys to better support mods with multiple traders in one trader area
[*]Version 0.4.18 and newer normalize legacy TXT destinations in memory and de-duplicate destination lists when old TXT and new JSON records refer to the same nearby trader
[*]Version 0.4.19 and newer separate trader identity from teleport destination position, so visiting the same trader from slightly different interaction spots no longer creates duplicate destinations
[*]Version 0.4.20 and newer abort travel when an unloaded destination still is not ready after preparation, with clearer server logs for diagnosis
[*]Version 0.4.21 and newer merge same-name destinations in the same trader area while still keeping different named traders in that area separate
[*]Version 0.4.22 and newer add friendly name mappings for Wasteland Mod traders Gene, Johnny, and Rad Cat
[*]Version 0.4.24 and newer also match compatible raw/internal trader ID variations and reuse existing matching records when recording visits, further reducing duplicate destinations from older data
[*]Before automatic JSON normalization, a one-time backup is created as VisitedTraderTeleportData.before-0.4.16.json
[/list]

[b]Extra safety tip[/b]
Before upgrading a server, stop the server and copy VisitedTraderTeleportData.json and VisitedTraderTeleportVisited.txt from the save folder first.

[b]Dedicated server note[/b]
Legacy data is read from the machine that owns the active save. Old TXT files that exist only on former clients are not transferred automatically.

[line]

[heading]Notes[/heading]

[list]
[*]The current trader is not shown as a teleport destination
[*]If there are no valid destinations, the destination screen explains that none are available in the current mode
[*]Teleport destinations are based on previously recorded trader visits
[*]The mod briefly prepares distant or unloaded destination areas before teleporting when needed
[*]If a destination cannot be prepared in time, travel is aborted and the server log explains which destination was not ready
[*]The client also refreshes destination visuals around teleport to reduce transparent POI objects after travel
[/list]
